# Case 6 (trivial static inline) is inlined: the callee body vanishes
# and the caller computes x+42 itself with no call.
absent \ntrivial:
in call_trivial: present lda 4,s\n\tclc\n\tadc\.w #42\n\trtl
# Since 2026-10-10 a static function is inlined, control flow and calls
# included, when it has one call site (case 1, the helper of case 3) or
# when it says `inline` (cases 2, 3, 5): none is left as a function, and
# no tail jump is left in the file (see auto_inline).
count 0 \tjml \w
raw absent \nno_kw\.
raw absent \nwith_if\.
raw absent \nhelper_for_nested\.
raw absent \nwith_nested_call\.
raw absent \ntoo_big\.
# Case 4, the recursive one: its body is copied once into its caller, and
# the call it makes to itself stays a real call to the function, kept.
raw present \nwith_recursion\.test_inline_boundaries:
in with_recursion: present jsl with_recursion
in call_with_recursion: present jsl with_recursion
